# dshx external plugin work

Use tools/dshx/knowledge/ by pointer: kb search finds an id; kb cat reads the contract. Before install/ship/HMR/reload/restart work, read contracts/live-activation and select exactly one branch with dshx activation-plan <plugin> --change patch|manifest|client|new-client|server|artifact.

- patch: watched config reconciliation, no Host restart.
- manifest: next-boot bundle state, Host restart.
- existing client: built lib/client.js HMR, no Host restart/page reload.
- new client: Host can stay up; reload/reopen the browser page.
- server: restart the current supervised Host unless exact module HMR is tested.
- artifact: synchronization only; activation unproven.

Required evidence flow: check → optional isolated verify-boot → optional sync-artifact → selected activation branch → Host/browser behavior proof. verify-boot may not stop a live Host. ship --restart is forbidden. restart-supervised targets only the current dshx-owned Web PID.

Never kill DSH from a Harness session, duplicate-mount a plugin, serve client source TSX, treat dump-config as live proof, or commit .env/.dshx/absolute machine paths.
